==================================================
ANIMATION SYSTEM
==================================================

Use Framer Motion.

Animations should support the design rather than distract from it.

Use:

- Fade-up entrance animations
- Subtle image reveal animations
- Staggered text animations
- Smooth section reveals
- Hover transitions
- Before/after slider interactions
- Subtle navbar transition on scroll

Avoid:

- Excessive bouncing
- Huge text rotations
- Random parallax everywhere
- Excessive blur
- Long loading animations
- Animations that slow down the experience

Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

If the user has reduced motion enabled, significantly reduce or disable decorative animations.

==================================================
IMAGE HANDLING
==================================================

For now, use placeholder image URLs or local placeholder assets.

Structure the image data separately from the UI components.

For example, create a portfolio data structure:

const projects = [
  {
    number: "01",
    title: "Portrait Retouching",
    description: "...",
    beforeImage: "...",
    afterImage: "..."
  },
  ...
]

This is VERY IMPORTANT.

Do not hardcode image URLs throughout the JSX.

I will replace the placeholder images with my real before/after images later.

Make replacing the images as simple as changing the image paths in one data file.

